#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087504 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63a7522-8d05-5d3a-aafb-3450292f910f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Components of a Linear Map"}] :question/id #uuid "ae56bd17-f7f2-5c66-ac2a-663f05c6a838" :question/math-academy-id "e-5518" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/bfdf3147fb8488c3a0032f9dad326b5d8c3ff68be46738dc39215e5098af6272.png)\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\to \\mathbb{R}^3$ shown above. What is the value of $a-b?$" :question/worked-solution "Given the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/35814ac6d965ac688907d162b45d9b0b194ea40375d4e474466e4fb4b1de1c1b.png) we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-8x-5y \\\\ -3x-6y \\\\ -4x+5y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5y-8x \\\\ -3x-6y \\\\ 5y-4x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/f59824c26875665fcbd8adfc5414fa7b0c60254e01f725f9ca72cf1d370a3e8b.png)\n\nFinally, $a-b=(-5)-(-4)=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087505 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb96cd29-b9f6-5b68-b43e-4a55ef8ffab2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map"}] :question/id #uuid "0ae354ba-19f3-570c-bbfc-56dd5dbbafa8" :question/math-academy-id "e-5519" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2,$ find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/7a6d4db6774da29f9b89996e348fad61b281737db6b44e9a39efa016fa2f15f3.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $\\,\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})=T\\cdot \\mathbf{v},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087519 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e35b58a-530f-5b9b-8df2-eb737f8af581" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "9c24c0bb-f779-5518-8c44-70b3e51065a2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5901" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that  represents  the  linear  transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2,$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/81d01f5d724e8b9d186bc53a15b488868c5c2d5d661f09d7c1febd862011afba.png)" :question/worked-solution "We require a $2\\times 3$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/412113c303aa31d5a9c23d5b0fa45201a8803b96f5239b9b1d007fc5128413c9.png)\n\nNotice that\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/bcd58c5310e4312fdbcc5619e0a89a03afb9bd5a6adff9a851e34d19e2bafb0b.png)\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n    ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/67da7147fc2e767f6c1fe15d2664d7f0b0e5f7b0778b168c6f702d2b999a2799.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335395 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63a7522-8d05-5d3a-aafb-3450292f910f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Components of a Linear Map"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "705bb233-0253-59bf-a5c2-fa2874395dee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335397} {:answer/id #uuid "751f0ab0-091c-5105-9343-764b504461e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335398} {:answer/id #uuid "4a2a502c-75a5-56c7-a6e0-218c1eb84c6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335399} {:answer/id #uuid "63d481f0-b30f-56f4-99e7-f5cec78dd844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335400} {:answer/id #uuid "d5e0cd58-e423-551b-91a5-891cfcc50dad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a2a502c-75a5-56c7-a6e0-218c1eb84c6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335399} :answer-field/id #uuid "f53b953b-0e7f-5c57-83d2-d0e5010d5d34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6c6739f-0bc4-58a0-97c1-be61353fa33d" :question/math-academy-id "q-140422" :question/problem "$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\,\\,T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}5x+4y \\\\ 3y+bx \\\\ -6x+cy\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ shown above. What is the value of $c+b?$" :question/worked-solution "Given the vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5x+4y \\\\ -x+3y \\\\ -6x+7y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5x+4y \\\\ 3y-x \\\\ -6x+7y\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}5x+4y \\\\ 3y+(-1)x \\\\ -6x+(7)y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $c+b=(-1)+7=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335402 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb96cd29-b9f6-5b68-b43e-4a55ef8ffab2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5907c55-befd-554b-8a83-e629b376573c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}26 \\\\ 17\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335404} {:answer/id #uuid "6bc4f599-759a-55a2-b755-cede8639df51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}19 \\\\ 25\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335405} {:answer/id #uuid "f4745e08-59cb-55d0-b4a2-86d2a9c0ee83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}23 \\\\ 19\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335406} {:answer/id #uuid "8e9573b3-f417-5700-b737-a7cb01a688ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}29 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335407} {:answer/id #uuid "0f4d085c-78b0-51df-b943-2961e39c6c20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}26 \\\\ 19\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f4d085c-78b0-51df-b943-2961e39c6c20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}26 \\\\ 19\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335408} :answer-field/id #uuid "e64a2cda-3735-5310-b7f8-12f33730f7eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335403}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "913716b3-e8d7-57a6-a016-07aa651d8ad6" :question/math-academy-id "q-140424" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2},$ find $T(v).$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -7\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}26 \\\\ 19\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335409 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb96cd29-b9f6-5b68-b43e-4a55ef8ffab2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "133f51db-922e-5449-988f-4c8abe348606" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 35\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335411} {:answer/id #uuid "a5829159-819e-5d16-9cd4-ecc3b95a1e5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335412} {:answer/id #uuid "ae8fc6c0-d6b3-5647-b9f3-a6005646f2e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 27\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335413} {:answer/id #uuid "85d26537-6708-52f7-9acf-0e70ab23f3d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335414} {:answer/id #uuid "33edf4e9-38bc-550d-8896-e72ebfeb1652" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 13 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5829159-819e-5d16-9cd4-ecc3b95a1e5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335412} :answer-field/id #uuid "63b198f9-9e5b-589f-9792-eb5eadf9dea7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335410}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e33fe2bb-6d66-5f91-becf-b6df459ced42" :question/math-academy-id "q-140425" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{4},$ find $T(v).$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -7\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088102 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb96cd29-b9f6-5b68-b43e-4a55ef8ffab2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b69459d5-3498-5323-9134-c7fc3e0185e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085544} {:answer/id #uuid "de6b3660-9bcc-55ab-8c64-7f1534ba5986" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085545} {:answer/id #uuid "15100286-887b-5cb4-aaf3-3ea9a1a0f87a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085546} {:answer/id #uuid "38486145-1630-5f9c-bd25-91e4ec0b1979" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085547} {:answer/id #uuid "5bc61647-6083-5c9c-8f5b-4f80c59826ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bc61647-6083-5c9c-8f5b-4f80c59826ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085548} :answer-field/id #uuid "301007b2-1548-5e5a-a4ce-94e854d05ae5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a30aa7a0-c30e-5f2f-9905-30e016a69140" :question/math-academy-id "q-38270" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3},$ find $T(v).$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088103 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63a7522-8d05-5d3a-aafb-3450292f910f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Components of a Linear Map"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e78cfed8-e425-53be-88cd-c049937dfd73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085550} {:answer/id #uuid "e9e29b72-96f1-502e-8771-eb85c27b9bb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085551} {:answer/id #uuid "105b0990-a386-53da-b33f-989bb74c8675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085552} {:answer/id #uuid "2a885e7f-935d-5bac-b04d-765925f8cede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085553} {:answer/id #uuid "36b383d4-31ad-52d6-a7e9-bf76318ef551" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a885e7f-935d-5bac-b04d-765925f8cede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085553} :answer-field/id #uuid "c26d6853-5ffc-5053-89db-cc64c23b1db4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5364abc3-dc71-58da-ac04-0528dba98c51" :question/math-academy-id "q-38271" :question/problem "$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}ay+2x-2z \\\\ bz-3x+cy\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2}$ shown above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Given the vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2x-3y-2z \\\\ -3x-y+4z\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3y+2x-2z \\\\ 4z-3x-y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-3y+2x-2z \\\\ 4z-3x+(-1)y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b+c=4+(-3)+(-1)=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088104 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63a7522-8d05-5d3a-aafb-3450292f910f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Components of a Linear Map"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1102a94-38ca-5664-a2e2-3cb1150548ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085556} {:answer/id #uuid "bac11e5f-5dc5-5fc4-8e18-3862fb8c267d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085557} {:answer/id #uuid "3019f51d-5016-5a2a-b353-b58fb684cfb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085558} {:answer/id #uuid "320d4836-4209-51ad-9e75-a4e3119e49b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085559} {:answer/id #uuid "6f46bd24-a2a1-557b-81cc-d3980c466440" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085560}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3019f51d-5016-5a2a-b353-b58fb684cfb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085558} :answer-field/id #uuid "a01483f4-6a03-52c4-9696-7a8534a1bf8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085555}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37118a2e-2a8e-5cb5-9d41-f658c8b8e89f" :question/math-academy-id "q-38272" :question/problem "$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -8 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-3x+y \\\\ ax-8y \\\\ -9x+by\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ shown above. What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "Given the vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -8 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3x+y \\\\ -2x-8y \\\\ -9x+7y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-3x+y \\\\ -2x-8y \\\\ -9x+7y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b=-2+7=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335416 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e35b58a-530f-5b9b-8df2-eb737f8af581" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acefcc6c-c888-54d6-9bfa-0972ca58f5bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335418} {:answer/id #uuid "ae0a1258-1b60-5257-852d-16ce3ddf37b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335419} {:answer/id #uuid "e57534a0-cb43-5646-912b-01712573ca64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335420} {:answer/id #uuid "ac061b1d-773a-503f-860b-7d45ec132355" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335421} {:answer/id #uuid "ae26d7e9-4745-5ffb-958d-8c1068b7b749" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acefcc6c-c888-54d6-9bfa-0972ca58f5bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335418} :answer-field/id #uuid "92d47e8a-1997-5b77-b646-f5ae2882eb0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4d6d3f76-538d-50cd-8960-d1a5eec76f1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-40450" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that  represents  the  linear  transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2},$ where\n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-3x-5y+2z \\\\ 2x-3y\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We require a $2\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}(-3)x+(-5)y+2z \\\\ 2x+(-3)y+0z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3x-5y+2z \\\\ 2x-3y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088324 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e35b58a-530f-5b9b-8df2-eb737f8af581" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9de48d64-d0d0-54b5-8b06-fb84a5f426ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086875} {:answer/id #uuid "e8da95b6-02ac-5768-8291-1c45536af869" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086876} {: